course: dictionary
lesson: 3222
title: Enter: going in, joining in, typing in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enter is one word with several meanings, so the words around it tell you which one you need. «The eye sees light that enters through the pupil.» Here enter means light goes into the eye.
explain: Enter can also mean to take part in something. «You cannot win a contest you never entered.» Here enter means you signed up to be in the contest. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: On a computer, enter means to type information in, like a password. The Enter key is the key you press to send or confirm what you have typed. If the words around enter talk about a keyboard or a screen, it means type it in.
explain: A sign that says «Do not enter» tells you not to go into that place. When you meet enter, try swapping in go into, join or type in. The one that makes sense is your meaning.
fact: Enter means to go or come into a place.
fact: To enter a competition or race means to take part in it.
fact: To enter information means to type or write it in, like entering a password.
fact: The Enter key is the key on a keyboard you press to send or confirm.
fact: «No entry» on a sign means you must not go in.
exercise: «The eye sees light that enters through the pupil.» What does enters mean here? | Moves away from | Makes a loud noise | *Goes into
exercise: «You cannot win a contest you never entered.» What does entered mean here? | *Signed up to take part in | Looked at carefully | Went into a room to watch | Typed a secret number
exercise: Which key on a keyboard sends or confirms what you have typed? | *The Enter key | The Tab key | The Shift key
test: «Do not enter» is written on the gate. What should you do? | Run inside to look | *Stay outside the gate | Walk through quickly | Climb over the wall
test: Ravi must enter his name on the race list. What does enter mean here? | Tear the list up | *Write it in to join | Leave the list | Read the names aloud
exam: Which word could replace enter in «The light enters the eye»? | Leaves | Sleeps | *Goes into | Hides
